blem 5 (C3)]] proposed by Merlijn Staps and Daniël Kroes, Netherlands\\n* [[2023 IMO Problems/Problem 6 | Problem 6 (G8)]] proposed by Ankan Bhattacharya and Luke Robitaille, USA\\n\\n== 2024 ==\\n\\n* [[2024 IMO]] (in UK)\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 1 | Problem 1 (A1)]] proposed by Santiago Rodríguez, Colombia\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 2 | Problem 2 (N4)]] proposed by Valentio Iverson, Indonesia\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 3 | Problem 3 (C7)]] proposed by Australia\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4 | Problem 4 (G2)]] proposed by Dominik Burek, Poland\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 5 | Problem 5 (C4)]] proposed by Cheuk Hei Chu, Hong Kong\\n* [[2024 IMO Problems/Problem 6 | Problem 6 (A7)]] proposed by Japan\\n\\n== 2025 ==\\n\\n* [[2025 IMO]] (in Australia)\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 1 | Problem 1 (C1)]] proposed by Linus Tang, USA\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 2 | Problem 2 (G4)]] proposed by Tran Quang Hung, Vietnam\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 3 | Problem 3 (N7)]] proposed by Lorenzo Sarria, Colombia\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 4 | Problem 4 (N3)]] proposed by Paulius Aleknavičius, Lithuania\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 5 | Problem 5 (A3)]] proposed by Massimiliano Foschi and Leonardo Franchi, Italy\\n* [[2025 IMO Problems/Problem 6 | Problem 6 (C8)]] proposed by Zhao Yu Ma and Daavid Lin Kewei, Singapore\\n\\n==2026==\\n\\n*[[2026 IMO]] (in China)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 1 | Problem 1]] (Giancarlo Kerg, Luxemburg)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 2 | Problem 2]] (Mykhailo Shtandenko, Ukraine)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 3 | Problem 3]] (Hya Bogdanov and Grigorii Chelnokov, Russia)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 4 | Problem 4]] (Switzerland)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 5 | Problem 5]] (Alfreds Sarocinskis, Latvia)\\n*[[2026 IMO Problems/Problem 6 | Problem 6]] (Hung-Hsun Hans Yu, Taiwan)\\n\\n== Comment ==\\n\\nThis page lists the authors and the proposing countries of the problems of the [[International Mathematical Olympiad|IMO]].\\n\\nFor many problems, the composers do not have the nationality of the proposing country. \\nFor instance, problem 2009/4 was proposed by Belgium, but only two of the three problem authors were Belgian, whereas the third is from South-Korea. Similarly, problem 2020/3 was proposed by Hungary with one Hungarian and one non-Hungarian problem author.\\n\\nTo the current moment, there is only a single IMO problem that has two distinct proposing countries: The if-part of problem 1994/2 was proposed by Australia and its only-if part by Armenia.\\n\\n== See also ==\\n\\n* [[IMO problems statistics]]  (eternal)\\n* [[IMO problems statistics since 2000]] (modern history)\\n* [https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c14_international_contests IMO problems on the Resources page]\\n* [[IMO Shortlist Problems]]\\n* [[Academic Olympiads]]\\n* [[Mathematics competition resources]]\\n\\n[[Category:Math Contest Problems]]\",\"USA TST Problems and Solutions\":\"Problems and solutions from the U.S.A. [[TST]]s.\\n\\n* [[2000 USA TST]]\\n* [[2001 USA TST]]\\n* [[2002 USA TST]]\\n* [[2003 USA TST]]\\n* [[2004 USA TST]]\\n\\n== Resources ==\\n\\n* [[MOP]]\\n* [[American Mathematics Competitions]]\\n* [[AMC Problems and Solutions]]\\n* [[Mathematics competition resources]]\\n\\n\\n[[Category:Math Contest Problems]]\",\"USAJMO Problems and Solutions\":\"[[USAJMO]] problems and solutions.\\n\\n*[[2026 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2025 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2024 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2023 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2022 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2021 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2020 USOJMO]]\\n*[[2019 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2018 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2017 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2016 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2015 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2014 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2013 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2012 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2011 USAJMO]]\\n*[[2010 USAJMO]]\"}"